{{!-- /the-faith-received/research/ — the research desk. One page, five
     workspaces, a tab strip under the heading, and whichever workspace
     is active fills everything below it.

     ROUTING. routes.yaml maps this template at
     /the-faith-received/research/. The deploy Action does NOT ship
     routes.yaml (FRONTEND §6.12) — it has to be uploaded by hand in
     Ghost Admin > Settings > Labs > Routes, and until it is, this URL
     404s no matter how healthy the template is.

     THE SHELL. assets/js/page/faith-research.js does the tab switching
     with the same mechanism faith-tfr-search.js's showMode() uses:
     [data-research-mode] buttons toggle `is-active`, [data-research-panel]
     elements toggle `hidden`. Deliberately its own small file rather
     than a sixth and seventh mode bolted onto faith-tfr-search.js —
     that file is 500-odd lines of Pagefind shard-merging and has no
     business knowing about this page. Deep-linkable: the hash (#ask,
     #power-search, #bookmarks, #notebook, #constellations) is read on
     load and written with replaceState on every tab change, same as
     the Search page.

     ASK. Renders partials/faith-received/_ask-panel.hbs — the SAME
     partial the standalone /the-faith-received/ask/ route and the Ask
     tab of /the-faith-received/search/ render. Not a copy: read that
     partial's header for the DOM contract assets/js/page/faith-ask.js
     binds to with unscoped querySelector() calls, and note the required
     script order (feature-gate.js, then page/faith-ask.js) reproduced
     at the bottom of this file. Nothing on this page may introduce a
     second [data-ask-*] element; faith-ask.js would bind to whichever
     came first in the document.

     POWER SEARCH. Semantic search over the corpus — meaning, not
     words. GET /v1/vsearch on mo-tfr-library (see
     website/workers/tfr-library/lib/vsearch.js for the response shape
     and the single-value `tradition` filter). Paid-member gated on the
     worker (requirePaidMember() in that worker's worker.js) and gated
     again client-side by the data-feature-gate="ask" on its submit
     button, per the standing rule that any LLM/embedding-spending
     feature carries both. Driven by assets/js/page/faith-power-search.js.

     BOOKMARKS / NOTEBOOK / CONSTELLATIONS. Empty on purpose. Bookmarks
     and Notebook are being built in a parallel session; Constellations
     is a port that does not exist yet. Each is a real panel with the
     right data-research-panel value and one honest line saying so, so
     the tab strip is complete and the panels are somewhere to drop
     real markup into. Nothing here fakes a feature. --}}

<main class="faith-received faith-feature">

  <section class="bhero bhero--tool">
    <div class="bhero-inner container">
      <p class="bhero-kicker"><a href="/the-faith-received/">The Faith Received</a> <span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span> <a href="/the-faith-received/research/">Research</a></p>
      <h1>Research</h1>
      <p class="bhero-sub">Nineteen thousand works of Christian theology, and the tools to work in them. Ask the library a question, search it by meaning, and keep what you find.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bband faith-feature-body faith-research-band">
    <div class="container" data-research-page>

      {{!-- The tab strip. Same markup and CSS as the Search page's mode
           tabs (.faith-view-toggle + .faith-search-modes overrides,
           which handle the horizontal scroll at 375px and the active
           tab's underline), with .faith-research-tabs adding only the
           rule that separates the strip from the workspace below it. --}}
      <nav class="faith-view-toggle faith-search-modes faith-research-tabs" data-research-tabs role="tablist" aria-label="Research workspace">
        <button type="button" class="faith-view-toggle-tab is-active" data-research-mode="ask" role="tab" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="research-panel-ask" id="research-tab-ask">Ask</button>
        <button type="button" class="faith-view-toggle-tab" data-research-mode="power-search" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="research-panel-power-search" id="research-tab-power-search">Power Search</button>
        <button type="button" class="faith-view-toggle-tab" data-research-mode="bookmarks" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="research-panel-bookmarks" id="research-tab-bookmarks">Bookmarks</button>
        <button type="button" class="faith-view-toggle-tab" data-research-mode="notebook" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="research-panel-notebook" id="research-tab-notebook">Notebook</button>
        <button type="button" class="faith-view-toggle-tab" data-research-mode="constellations" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="research-panel-constellations" id="research-tab-constellations">Constellations</button>
      </nav>

      {{!-- ── Ask ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
           The shared partial, unmodified. .ask-workspace inside it
           breaks out of this .container and runs the full width of the
           viewport on its own white ground (percentage margins, so it
           works from any parent width) — which is exactly the
           "workspace fills the section below the bar" shape this page
           is built around, and the reason Power Search below uses the
           same shell. --}}
      <div data-research-panel="ask" data-ask-page role="tabpanel" id="research-panel-ask" aria-labelledby="research-tab-ask">
        {{> "faith-received/_ask-panel"}}
      </div>

      {{!-- ── Power Search ───────────────────────────────────────────
           The control sits at the TOP of this workspace rather than
           docked at the bottom the way Ask's composer is, and that is
           deliberate rather than an oversight. Ask is one question and
           one long answer, so its composer is the last thing you touch
           and the answer scrolls up past it. Search is iterative: you
           read a list, narrow the tradition, rephrase, run it again.
           Burying the box under twenty hits would make every refinement
           a scroll to the bottom of the page. Same composer geometry
           and the same dark button, so the register still matches;
           only the position differs.

           DOM contract for assets/js/page/faith-power-search.js. Every
           querySelector in that file is listed here:
             - form[data-ps-form] > input[data-ps-input],
               button[data-ps-submit]
             - [data-ps-scope] wrapping [data-ps-scope-state] and the
               [data-ps-tradition] pills
             - [data-ps-status], [data-ps-error], [data-ps-empty],
               [data-ps-results], [data-ps-noresults], [data-ps-count]
             - [data-ps-filters] wrapping [data-ps-filters-state],
               [data-ps-narrow], [data-ps-facets], [data-ps-clear]
             - [data-ps-filter-status], [data-ps-nomatch] wrapping
               [data-ps-nomatch-note], [data-ps-ceiling]
             - [data-ps-pager] wrapping [data-ps-prev],
               [data-ps-page-label], [data-ps-next]
           The chips inside [data-ps-facets] are built in JS, not here:
           their values are whatever the works on screen happen to be,
           so there is no fixed vocabulary to write down.
           The submit button carries data-feature-gate="ask" so
           feature-gate.js intercepts a free or anonymous visitor's
           click before it ever reaches the submit handler. Do not
           remove it: the worker enforces the same gate server-side, but
           the modal is the only thing that tells a non-member WHY
           nothing happened.

           The nine tradition values must stay byte-identical to
           KNOWN_TRADITIONS in website/workers/tfr-library/lib/ask.js
           (the same nine Ask's scope control offers). vsearch's filter
           is an exact-match Vectorize metadata filter, so a value that
           does not match reads as "the filter found nothing" rather
           than as an error. Single-select, not multi-select like Ask's:
           /v1/vsearch takes ONE `tradition` param (see handleVSearch in
           lib/vsearch.js), so a multi-select control here would be
           promising something the endpoint cannot do. --}}
      <div data-research-panel="power-search" role="tabpanel" id="research-panel-power-search" aria-labelledby="research-tab-power-search" hidden>
        <div class="research-workspace" data-ps-workspace>
          <div class="research-workspace-inner">
           <div class="research-column">

            <div class="ps-controls">
              <form class="ps-form" data-ps-form>
                <label class="visually-hidden" for="ps-query">Search the library by meaning</label>
                <input
                  id="ps-query"
                  class="ps-input"
                  type="search"
                  data-ps-input
                  maxlength="300"
                  autocomplete="off"
                  placeholder="Describe the idea you are looking for&hellip;"
                  required
                />
                <button type="submit" class="ps-submit" data-feature-gate="ask" data-ps-submit>Search</button>
              </form>

              {{!-- Collapsed by default. The whole library is the right
                   default and a wall of ten pills above the results
                   would dominate the workspace before anything has been
                   searched. faith-power-search.js writes the summary
                   line so the collapsed state still says what is
                   selected — a filter set and forgotten silently
                   narrows every later search otherwise. --}}
              <details class="ps-scope" data-ps-scope>
                <summary class="ps-scope-summary">
                  <span class="ps-scope-title">Scope</span>
                  <span class="ps-scope-state" data-ps-scope-state>The whole library</span>
                </summary>
                <div class="ps-scope-body">
                  <p class="ps-scope-legend" id="ps-scope-tradition-label">Tradition</p>
                  <div class="ps-scope-pills" role="group" aria-labelledby="ps-scope-tradition-label">
                    <button type="button" class="faith-filter-pill is-active" data-ps-tradition="" aria-pressed="true">The whole library</button>
                    <button type="button" class="faith-filter-pill" data-ps-tradition="English Divines" aria-pressed="false">English Divines</button>
                    <button type="button" class="faith-filter-pill" data-ps-tradition="Greek Fathers" aria-pressed="false">Greek Fathers</button>
                    <button type="button" class="faith-filter-pill" data-ps-tradition="Humanism and Law" aria-pressed="false">Humanism and Law</button>
                    <button type="button" class="faith-filter-pill" data-ps-tradition="Lutheran" aria-pressed="false">Lutheran</button>
                    <button type="button" class="faith-filter-pill" data-ps-tradition="Medieval" aria-pressed="false">Medieval</button>
                    <button type="button" class="faith-filter-pill" data-ps-tradition="Latin Fathers" aria-pressed="false">Latin Fathers</button>
                    <button type="button" class="faith-filter-pill" data-ps-tradition="Eastern Fathers" aria-pressed="false">Eastern Fathers</button>
                    <button type="button" class="faith-filter-pill" data-ps-tradition="Roman Catholic" aria-pressed="false">Roman Catholic</button>
                    <button type="button" class="faith-filter-pill" data-ps-tradition="Reformed" aria-pressed="false">Reformed</button>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </details>
            </div>

            <p class="ps-status" data-ps-status role="status" aria-live="polite" hidden></p>
            <p class="ps-error" data-ps-error role="alert" hidden></p>

            {{!-- Empty state. The example searches only fill the box;
                  they never submit. A search spends a real embedding
                  call and the paid-member gate lives on the submit
                  button's own click, so nothing here may reach the
                  worker on its own. --}}
            <div class="ps-empty" data-ps-empty>
              <p class="ps-empty-lede">Search by what a passage means, not by the words it happens to use.</p>
              <p class="ps-empty-note">A search for God&rsquo;s unchangeableness finds the passage that says immutability and never uses the word. Ask for an idea in your own English and the library answers in Latin, Greek and four centuries of English prose.</p>
              <ul class="ps-examples">
                <li><button type="button" class="ps-example" data-ps-example>justification by faith alone</button></li>
                <li><button type="button" class="ps-example" data-ps-example>the real presence in the eucharist</button></li>
                <li><button type="button" class="ps-example" data-ps-example>how the will is bound before grace</button></li>
              </ul>
            </div>

            {{!-- Filters. A DIFFERENT control from Scope above, and the
                  copy has to keep saying so: Scope decides what gets
                  searched and costs a new query, these narrow the works
                  already on screen and cost nothing. They sit below the
                  count and above the list because that is where the
                  thing they act on is (UX §3b.5, action proximity).

                  Hidden until a search returns. The chip groups inside
                  [data-ps-facets] are written by the JS from the result
                  set itself, and a group only appears when the results
                  hold at least two distinct values for it. --}}
            <details class="ps-filters" data-ps-filters hidden>
              <summary class="ps-filters-summary">
                <span class="ps-filters-title">Filter</span>
                <span class="ps-filters-state" data-ps-filters-state></span>
              </summary>
              <div class="ps-filters-body">
                <p class="ps-filters-note">These narrow the works already found. They do not run a new search.</p>

                <div class="ps-narrow-field">
                  <label class="ps-facet-legend" for="ps-narrow">Author or title</label>
                  <input id="ps-narrow" class="ps-narrow" type="search" data-ps-narrow maxlength="120" autocomplete="off" />
                </div>

                <div class="ps-facets" data-ps-facets></div>

                <button type="button" class="ps-clear" data-ps-clear hidden>Clear filters</button>
              </div>
            </details>

            {{!-- The filters announce what they left. A reader using a
                  screen reader gets no signal at all from twenty-five
                  rows silently becoming nine. --}}
            <p class="visually-hidden" data-ps-filter-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>

            {{!-- tabindex="-1" so the pager can put focus here. A pager
                  that swaps twenty-five rows and leaves focus on a Next
                  button that may have just gone disabled loses a
                  keyboard reader entirely; this line has been rewritten
                  to say exactly where they now are. --}}
            <p class="ps-count" data-ps-count tabindex="-1" hidden></p>
            <ol class="ps-results" data-ps-results hidden></ol>

            {{!-- "The library found nothing" and "you filtered it all
                  away" are an identical empty list and opposite facts,
                  so they are two states with two different sentences
                  (FRONTEND §6.33). --}}
            <div class="ps-nomatch" data-ps-nomatch hidden>
              <p class="ps-noresults-lede">No works match these filters.</p>
              <p class="ps-noresults-note" data-ps-nomatch-note></p>
            </div>

            <nav class="ps-pager" data-ps-pager aria-label="Result pages" hidden>
              <button type="button" class="ps-pager-btn" data-ps-prev>Previous</button>
              <span class="ps-pager-label" data-ps-page-label></span>
              <button type="button" class="ps-pager-btn" data-ps-next>Next</button>
            </nav>

            {{!-- The ceiling, said out loud. Vectorize returns at most
                  fifty candidate passages when metadata comes back with
                  them, so a work-grouped list tops out around forty and
                  can never run to a third page. Better to state that
                  than to let a reader read a short list as the library
                  having little to say. --}}
            <p class="ps-ceiling" data-ps-ceiling hidden>Power Search reads the fifty closest passages in the library and groups them into works, so this is a shortlist rather than every match. Change the scope above, or ask for the idea a different way, to reach further in.</p>

            <div class="ps-noresults" data-ps-noresults hidden>
              <p class="ps-noresults-lede">Nothing close enough to that.</p>
              <p class="ps-noresults-note">Try describing the idea a different way, or widen the tradition above. The semantic index is still being built out across the collections, so a corner of the library may not answer yet.</p>
            </div>

           </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      {{!-- ── Bookmarks / Notebook / Constellations ──────────────────
           Deliberately empty. Bookmarks and Notebook are under
           construction in a parallel session and Constellations has not
           been ported yet; each panel says so in one line and does
           nothing else.

           Each still carries the same three-div workspace shell the
           other two tabs use (.research-workspace > -inner >
           .research-column) so that switching tabs doesn't change the
           ground under the reader's feet, and so whoever builds these
           out replaces one .faith-pending-panel with real markup and
           inherits the layout for free. Keep the
           data-research-panel attribute where it is —
           faith-research.js reads nothing else about these panels. --}}
      <div data-research-panel="bookmarks" role="tabpanel" id="research-panel-bookmarks" aria-labelledby="research-tab-bookmarks" hidden>
        <div class="research-workspace">
          <div class="research-workspace-inner">
           {{> "faith-received/_bookmarks-panel"}}
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div data-research-panel="notebook" role="tabpanel" id="research-panel-notebook" aria-labelledby="research-tab-notebook" hidden>
        <div class="research-workspace">
          <div class="research-workspace-inner">
           {{> "faith-received/_notebook-panel"}}
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div data-research-panel="constellations" role="tabpanel" id="research-panel-constellations" aria-labelledby="research-tab-constellations" hidden>
        <div class="research-workspace">
          <div class="research-workspace-inner">
           {{> "faith-received/_constellations-panel"}}
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  {{!-- No prices here on purpose: /membership/ is where they live, and a
       number repeated in two places is a number that goes stale in one. --}}
  <section class="bband bband--cream faith-tools">
    <div class="container">
      <header class="bhead">
        <p class="blabel">For members</p>
        <h2>Get the most from The Faith Received.</h2>
      </header>
      <ul class="blist blist--2 blist--tools">
        <li><span class="brow-t">Ask</span><span class="brow-m">A question answered from the corpus. Every page it drew on is cited inline.</span></li>
        <li><span class="brow-t">Power Search</span><span class="brow-m">Search by meaning rather than by word, across every collection.</span></li>
        <li><span class="brow-t">Latin word forms</span><span class="brow-m">One search across every inflection of a word.</span></li>
        <li><span class="brow-t">Constellations</span><span class="brow-m">The passages that stand behind a passage. Share the set as a link.</span></li>
        <li><span class="brow-t">Citation export</span><span class="brow-m">Copy, permalink, BibTeX or Zotero. Each one carries its locus.</span></li>
        <li><span class="brow-t">The notebook</span><span class="brow-m">Highlight a paragraph, keep a private note, or write your own translation.</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

<section class="faith-join">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="blabel">Become a member</p>
    <h2>Use the tools and support the work.</h2>
      <div class="toggle-wrap" role="tablist" aria-label="Billing interval">
        <div class="toggle">
          <button type="button" class="toggle-option is-active" data-interval="annual" role="tab" aria-selected="true" data-hm-goal="plan-annual">
            Annual
            <span class="badge">Save 17%</span>
          </button>
          <button type="button" class="toggle-option" data-interval="monthly" role="tab" aria-selected="false" data-hm-goal="plan-monthly">Monthly</button>
        </div>
      </div>
  </div>
</section>

{{> "membership-pricing"}}
</main>
{{> "membership-cta"}}

<script src="{{asset "js/page/membership-toggle.js"}}"></script>
<script src="{{asset "js/page/membership-cards.js"}}"></script>

{{!-- feature-gate.js FIRST, then the two page scripts that depend on
     it gating their submit buttons — the same relative order
     custom-faith-ask.hbs and custom-faith-search.hbs use for the same
     partial. All three are plain page-bottom <script src> tags rather
     than bundle members because page-template scripts run BEFORE
     site.min.js (FRONTEND §6.18); the only bundle global any of them
     touches is window.MOAuth, which ships in boot.min.js in <head> and
     is therefore already on the page. --}}
<script src="{{asset "js/feature-gate.js"}}"></script>
<script src="{{asset "js/page/faith-ask.js"}}"></script>
<script src="{{asset "js/page/faith-power-search.js"}}"></script>
<script src="{{asset "js/page/faith-research.js"}}"></script>

<script src="{{asset "js/faith-gate.js"}}"></script>
